Subject: [PATCH] Lichii #1094: command lists on GPU-written pages read the words no GPU work wrote from guest memory, DMAClear checks its whole range (EDEN_UP_L1094_LIST_WORDS, EDEN_UP_L1094_DMACLEAR, EDEN_UP_L1094_STATS; all off by default)

Port of zortos293/Lichii #1094 (jpkto, open; "video_core: wait less for the writers of command
lists", #805's lists 18 = 34656e8225 and 43 = d4e8d85d4d). On top of T85 (0001..0486).

Mapped against T85 (have / partly / missing; T85 line numbers):
- DMACopy notes its guest write to command list pages (34656e8225): have, EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DMALIST
  (0453), buffer_cache.h:1303-1311.
- DMAClear checks its whole range (`amount` counts words, the check took it as bytes) and notes
  its guest write (34656e8225): have, EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DMALIST (0453), buffer_cache.h:1362-1378,
  both halves behind one switch.
- Command list pages track the words GPU work wrote; lists on none of them read guest memory, copy
  reads take the other words from guest memory (34656e8225, Fritchii's EXP40 word reads): missing.
  0474 left it out by name. T85's Nx2ListPage (buffer_cache_base.h:1258) counts writes per page
  only; Nx2ReadListCopy (buffer_cache.h:3854) is Synced only when the whole page is.
- An entry that begins between methods skips the writer wait while no copy engine work is queued
  (d4e8d85d4d): have, EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_LISTSKIP (0474): dma_pusher.cpp:552, CopyWritersPending
  gpu_split.h:542, NoteCopyWriter dma_pusher.cpp:1403/1475. The same rule as upstream's
  `command_entry && !CopyWritersPending`; ours waits by the active list rule when it does wait.
- The wait before a list on a GPU-written page goes to the writers before the last sync, new
  site "list copy writers" (d4e8d85d4d): missing. T85 waits for every writer there
  (dma_pusher.cpp:1922, site "list gpu-written"). Not ported, see below.
- BufferCacheRuntime::WaitSubmittedTick publishes the front's words before it waits for a copy:
  missing (vk_buffer_cache.cpp:566). Not ported, see below.

Against LISTSYNC (0474) and the 0485 list fetch rules: those set how long an entry on a page NOT
known GPU-written waits for queued compute and copy work (the "list writers" site). LIST_WORDS
acts later and elsewhere: only on entries on pages already GPU-written and marked as command list
pages, after their own writer wait ("list gpu-written", unchanged), on what they read (copy, guest
memory, or drain and flush). Complementary, no shared state beyond the page entries; any of them
can be on together. LIST_WORDS does not move the "list writers" wait at all.

What each switch does (Common::PeSwitch, exactly "1"; read once):
EDEN_UP_L1094_LIST_WORDS=1: each command list page keeps a bitset of its 4-byte words GPU work
  wrote that guest memory lacks: set for the whole range each noted dispatch or copy write may
  cover (Nx2NoteListWrite), cleared for the words a host write covers whole (Nx2NoteListHostWrite:
  CPU, inline and, with this switch, DMACopy/DMAClear writes) and for all words when the front
  flushed the page (Nx2NoteListSynced, which also marks the page `flushed`). In Nx2ReadListCopy a
  list on a flushed page draws never wrote, on none of those words, returns Synced: the front reads
  guest memory, waits for no copy and does not drain and flush. A copy read on a flushed page
  takes only the GPU-written words from the copy and the others from guest memory (a CPU write the
  buffer had not uploaded when the copy was made is no longer read stale from the copy). It also
  turns on DMALIST's two DMACopy/DMAClear notes (as upstream), not DMALIST's range fix.
EDEN_UP_L1094_DMACLEAR=1: DMAClear's buffer check covers the whole range, without DMALIST's
  notes. A plain bug fix, but it changes behaviour: a clear whose registered buffer lies past the
  first quarter of its range now also clears the GPU buffer (before, only guest memory got it,
  through MaxwellDMA's unsafe write, and the buffer kept the old words). It adds a GPU clear, no
  waits. DMALIST keeps doing both halves.
EDEN_UP_L1094_STATS=1 (any arm, the control included; no behaviour change, the words are then
  tracked so each list gets the verdict LIST_WORDS would give) logs every 10 s from the front:
  "Lichii #1094 in 10 s (EDEN_UP_L1094_LIST_WORDS=, EDEN_UP_L1094_DMACLEAR=): lists on
  GPU-written command list pages R: S on pages guest memory holds whole, C checked by word (W
  words): K on no word GPU work wrote (read from guest memory | would read guest memory with
  LIST_WORDS; on the copy path now: A waited for their copy (X ms), B without a current copy);
  copy path: F copies ready, T copy waits (Y ms), U without a current copy (drain and flush) or
  pending, M copy reads merged with guest memory; DMA clears N: Q registered past the old quarter
  check". K = list waits skipped because no written word was touched, F+T+U = kept, W = words
  checked. In the control, A/X/B are what LIST_WORDS would save; with LIST_WORDS on they are 0.
  The start line "Lichii #1094: EDEN_UP_L1094_LIST_WORDS=..." shows the switches as read.

Unset (all three): T85 behaviour. What still runs: a static switch test per noted list page write,
host write and flush, three no-op counter calls and one switch test per list read, a time_point
default in the copy wait path, a switch test per DMACopy/DMAClear; Nx2ListPage grows by a
1,024-bit bitset and a bool per command list page.

Not ported:
- d4e8d85d4d's narrower wait before lists on GPU-written pages (ReadGpuWrittenCommands: every
  writer -> the writers before the last sync, site "list copy writers"). In the T85 walk control
  (t85-b run684) that whole site is "list gpu-written" 0.1-0.2 ms/s at 159-268 waits/s: nothing to
  gain on this route, and it would read lists whose writer is still queued with no miss check.
  Worth porting with a back-side check once a route (Death Mountain: upstream's 99.6 ms/s) shows it.
- WaitSubmittedTick's Publish before a copy wait: the copy path is ~80 lists/s here (FETCH_COUNT
  "GPU-written page, host copy" 8,862 in ~110 s of run684); what its waits cost is not measured
  yet. The STATS line's copy waits (T, Y ms) measure it; port it if they are worth it.
- The tests (buffer_cache_ports.cpp): our tests are not built.
- Upstream's draw-written pages after a host sync (past_sync / NeedsSync): T85 has none of that
  base; draw-written pages keep draining here, with or without the switch.

Risks:
- LIST_WORDS: a GPU write that reaches a list page without Nx2NoteListWrite (a path that marks the
  page GPU-written some other way) would leave its words clear, and a list on them would read guest
  memory without the write: a stale list can lose the device or hang. Every noted path is the one
  T85's copies already rely on (MarkWrittenBuffer for dispatches, DMACopy's mirror), and the words
  are only trusted on pages the front flushed once. A draw's first write to a page still queued
  when a list there is read is missed exactly as T85's Synced and copy paths miss it today.
- DMACLEAR: one more GPU clear per affected DMA clear; the STATS line counts them (Q).

